WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.495 --> 00:00:03.495
(missile whooshing)

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.850
- Joint exercises between the
US and Philippine militaries

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.860
are just wrapping up
out here in the Pacific.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.110
And while these exercises
happen every year,

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.693
this year marked the
biggest show of force ever.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.610
Right now, we're watching a drone fly laps

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:21.960
off the coast of this beach,

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.490
and behind me is an Avenger platform

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.900
loaded with stinger missiles

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.700
that are gonna take down that drone.

00:00:27.868 --> 00:00:30.390
(missile whooshing)

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.710
- Our task is to be ready

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.930
with defensive weapon systems like this.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.120
Certainly, this is a great
opportunity to do that

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.670
for US soldiers and our leaders.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.650
We wouldn't be here unless
it was at the request

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.080
of our partners through the Philippines,

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.710
and it demonstrates not
only a real capability

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.380
should it be required, but
hopefully it demonstrates

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.900
to our partners a special relationship

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:55.209
as one of our five treaty
alliances that we have out here.

00:00:55.209 --> 00:00:57.792
(gentle music)

00:01:04.257 --> 00:01:08.417
(gentle music continues)

00:01:08.417 --> 00:01:11.584
(helicopter whirring)

00:01:18.943 --> 00:01:22.360
(gentle music continues)

00:01:31.063 --> 00:01:33.912
(gentle music continues)

00:01:33.912 --> 00:01:37.621
(helicopter whirring)

00:01:37.621 --> 00:01:39.420
- These exercises are coming on the heels

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.690
of a major new agreement that's
giving the US greater access

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:44.611
to Philippine bases.

00:01:44.611 --> 00:01:47.278
(fanfare music)

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:54.840
- [Participant] The US being the biggest

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.390
or one of the biggest players
in the West Philippine Sea.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:59.250
- These efforts are especially important

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.500
as people's Republic of China

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:05.640
continues to advance
its illegitimate claims

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.543
in the West Philippine Sea.

00:02:07.543 --> 00:02:09.438
(gentle music)

00:02:09.438 --> 00:02:12.605
(helicopter whirring)

00:02:16.396 --> 00:02:19.590
(gentle music continues)

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.630
- I'm confident that
regardless of the threat,

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:25.290
my responsibility is to train
our shoulders to be prepared.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:28.050
We demonstrated some of
that capability out here

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.483
during this live fire.

00:02:29.483 --> 00:02:31.290
(missile whooshing)

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.975
Our opportunity and our responsibility

00:02:33.975 --> 00:02:35.310
and our mission is to defeat a range

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:37.010
of threats if those are presented.

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:39.540
- Following these exercises,

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:40.770
the president of the Philippines

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.020
is heading to the White House
to meet with President Biden

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.210
to talk about their commitment to defense

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:47.190
and other ways the
countries can work together

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:49.443
like potential economic cooperation.

00:02:50.312 --> 00:02:53.729
(gentle music continues)

